1
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:12,639
I’m sorry for the trouble earlier, Comrade Roong.

2
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:13,959
Especially now that Comrade Fah has forbidden-

3
00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:15,119
-anyone from entering or leaving the base.

4
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:16,879
But that household is in serious condition.

5
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:18,799
That’s why we had to ask you to come help.

6
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:21,359
It’s alright. The villagers’ lives are what matter most.

7
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:23,656
If there’s any problem, I’ll speak with Comrade Fah myself.

8
00:00:23,680 --> 00:00:24,839
Um... Comrade Roong.

9
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:25,840
We’d better go this way.

10
00:00:25,841 --> 00:00:27,976
There are too many people that way. Someone might see us.

11
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,240
If we go this way, we won’t run into Comrade Fah either.

12
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:39,120
Ever since Comrade Ploeng died,

13
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:41,200
the base has felt so quiet and lonely.

14
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:44,920
How has Comrade Bai Tong been lately?

15
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:48,600
She barely ate foods I gave her.

16
00:00:51,480 --> 00:00:52,480
Comrade Gaun Hin.

17
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:53,959
Where are you going?

18
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:55,919
Oh, I’m taking documents for the courier-

19
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:57,400
-to deliver for printing in the city.

20
00:00:58,280 --> 00:00:59,280
Go and come back quickly.

21
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:00,480
Be careful.

22
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:03,840
Comrades

23
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,919
we caught the person who killed Ploeng.

24
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:06,999
Comrades.

25
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,400
Comrades, we caught the person who killed Ploeng.

26
00:01:57,280 --> 00:01:58,560
Mm.

27
00:02:03,520 --> 00:02:04,520
Dan.

28
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:09,280
Answer whatever I ask.

29
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:11,440
Because if you talk,

30
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:14,119
you won’t have to get hurt.

31
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:15,120
Mm.

32
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:16,200
Comrade Fah! Comrade Fah!

33
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:17,720
Comrade Fah.

34
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:19,280
Comrade Fah.

35
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:21,799
Comrade Roong is gone.

36
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:22,960
Since when?

37
00:02:23,480 --> 00:02:24,440
Yang Sue said

38
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:25,360
a villager was in critical condition

39
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:26,280
and urgently needed medicine.

40
00:02:26,281 --> 00:02:27,521
So Roong rushed out right away.

41
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:30,320
I told her to stay inside the base.

42
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:33,159
And where is Yang Sue now?

43
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:35,319
The villagers said he left with the cabbage truck

44
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:36,560
before sunrise.

45
00:02:38,640 --> 00:02:39,960
And now Comrade Roong is missing.

46
00:02:40,640 --> 00:02:41,720
Don’t tell anyone yet.

47
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:46,680
I don’t want the people in the village to panic.

48
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:55,960
Whoa...

49
00:02:56,440 --> 00:02:57,600
that was close.

50
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:00,160
Just now, Comrade Yue seemed to turn

51
00:03:00,161 --> 00:03:01,439
and look this way too.

52
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:03,000
Not sure if he saw us or not.

53
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:06,480
Sorry, I lost myself for a second.

54
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:08,720
This guy...

55
00:03:08,721 --> 00:03:10,519
he’s probably the one who killed Comrade Ploeng.

56
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:12,039
You know him too?

57
00:03:12,040 --> 00:03:12,960
Yes.

58
00:03:12,961 --> 00:03:14,401
He was my neighbor when I was a kid.

59
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:18,279
Doesn’t matter how you know him.

60
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:19,959
You’d better stay away from him.

61
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:21,520
You might get dragged into it too.

62
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:24,600
Hey, Comrade Saeng.

63
00:03:24,880 --> 00:03:27,320
Don’t even think about going to see Dan, Comrade Saeng.

64
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:30,000
Go on, get going.

65
00:03:45,160 --> 00:03:46,520
What brings you here, Comrade?

66
00:03:47,320 --> 00:03:49,240
Or do you need some medicine?

67
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:52,800
I came to get supplies to treat the prisoner’s gunshot wound.

68
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:54,240
Get them ready for me.

69
00:03:55,760 --> 00:03:56,760
Yes.

70
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:13,199
And...

71
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:15,759
Are you going to remove the bullet yourself?

72
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:17,320
Would you like me to do it for you?

73
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:20,160
It’s alright.

74
00:04:21,480 --> 00:04:22,480
I’ll take it out myself.

75
00:04:30,640 --> 00:04:31,640
Comrade Yue.

76
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:34,280
Comrade Ying.

77
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:35,959
I came to speak with you about-

78
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:37,400
-my mother’s condition for a moment.

79
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:40,480
How is she?

80
00:04:40,880 --> 00:04:41,920
Has she gotten any better?

81
00:04:42,960 --> 00:04:44,160
We got medicine from the base,

82
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:46,240
so we’ve managed to keep her stable.

83
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:54,520
It’s done.

84
00:04:58,840 --> 00:05:00,919
Has he admitted yet that he was-

85
00:05:00,920 --> 00:05:02,320
-the one who killed Comrade Ploeng?

86
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:08,360
Not yet.

87
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:11,760
A son of a high-ranking military officer like you.

88
00:06:13,320 --> 00:06:15,600
Why would you choose to be stationed here?

89
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:18,680
What do you want?

90
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:36,240
Getting yourself captured like this...

91
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:40,040
Was it your plan?

92
00:06:58,040 --> 00:06:59,800
Comrade Roong disappearance...

93
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:04,000
That was because of you too, wasn’t it?

94
00:07:44,640 --> 00:07:46,080
Whatever you’re hoping for,

95
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:51,280
you won’t get your way.

96
00:07:54,120 --> 00:07:55,120
You still don’t know

97
00:07:56,720 --> 00:07:58,200
who’s going to be disappointed.

98
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:46,240
Vin.

99
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:47,240
Dan.

100
00:08:53,800 --> 00:08:55,120
How did you end up here?

101
00:08:57,640 --> 00:08:58,640
I came here on purpose.

102
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:00,720
I wanted to see you, Vin.

103
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:04,880
Aunt La-Or feels the same.

104
00:09:05,520 --> 00:09:07,600
She misses you so much she’s fallen sick many times.

105
00:09:08,640 --> 00:09:09,680
She told me

106
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:12,200
to bring you home no matter what.

107
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:17,039
But it’s not that easy, Dan.

108
00:09:17,040 --> 00:09:18,040
It’s not that hard, Vin.

109
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:20,720
Just say the word,

110
00:09:21,840 --> 00:09:23,200
and I’ll take you out myself.

111
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:28,160
Worry about saving yourself first.

112
00:09:29,120 --> 00:09:29,760
Get up.

113
00:09:29,761 --> 00:09:31,239
Hey! Let go of Vin!

114
00:09:31,240 --> 00:09:32,240
Stay out of this.

115
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:33,640
Don’t touch my people.

116
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:35,480
Vin.

117
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:38,119
Can I have five minutes? Just five minutes.

118
00:09:38,120 --> 00:09:39,120
Five minutes?

119
00:09:39,840 --> 00:09:41,239
That could get you killed.

120
00:09:41,240 --> 00:09:42,360
What if someone else sees?

121
00:09:42,960 --> 00:09:44,080
Have you thought about that?

122
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:45,760
Hey!

123
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:53,440
What were you doing in there?

124
00:09:59,240 --> 00:10:00,440
Treating the prisoner's wound.

125
00:10:00,760 --> 00:10:01,800
I forgot something inside.

126
00:10:05,280 --> 00:10:06,280
Where is it then?

127
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:10,520
It wasn't there.

128
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:14,399
I dropped it somewhere else.

129
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:16,040
Then why did you come together?

130
00:10:20,240 --> 00:10:21,560
And what rule says.

131
00:10:22,560 --> 00:10:23,800
Two people can’t come together?

132
00:10:52,480 --> 00:10:54,120
What are you with that soldier?

133
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,000
He was a neighbor.

134
00:10:56,760 --> 00:10:58,240
We knew each other when we were kids.

135
00:10:59,040 --> 00:11:01,240
But he moved away when I was still in primary school.

136
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:03,960
We never spoke again after that.

137
00:11:13,640 --> 00:11:15,440
That one is like an older brother.

138
00:11:21,640 --> 00:11:23,880
But this one isn’t.

139
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:29,480
Promise me

140
00:11:30,560 --> 00:11:32,000
you won’t go see that soldier again.

141
00:11:34,520 --> 00:11:37,320
If anyone finds out, it’ll be very dangerous.

142
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:47,640
Let me help you then.

143
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:51,800
Get this over with.

144
00:12:23,760 --> 00:12:25,440
May I hold your hand?

145
00:12:37,520 --> 00:12:38,760
Who is Aunt La-Or?

146
00:12:39,640 --> 00:12:40,720
My mother.

147
00:12:45,280 --> 00:12:47,200
There’s still a lot about you that I don’t know.

148
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:50,520
Not knowing isn’t a problem.

149
00:12:51,720 --> 00:12:53,400
We still have our whole lives together.

150
00:12:53,920 --> 00:12:57,200
I will tell you little by little, and you can teach me too.

151
00:13:03,080 --> 00:13:04,920
Everything I know, I’ve already taught you.

152
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:15,680
Except this... You still have a lot to teach me.

153
00:13:28,200 --> 00:13:29,280
Pack up quickly.

154
00:13:37,880 --> 00:13:39,199
I just found out-

155
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:41,959
-that grinding stones and mixing them with honey

156
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:43,760
can make a color like this.

157
00:13:46,280 --> 00:13:47,760
If I put this on for Father to see,

158
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:50,480
he’d definitely say I look cute.

159
00:14:00,120 --> 00:14:02,280
Comrade Ploeng hasn’t gone far at all.

160
00:14:03,080 --> 00:14:04,360
He only changed where he lives—.

161
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:07,600
Now he lives in Comrade Bai Tong’s heart.

162
00:14:08,880 --> 00:14:11,999
And you still have us, you have Comrade Saeng,

163
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:14,400
and all the comrades beside you too.

164
00:14:25,080 --> 00:14:26,360
What are you doing here?

165
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:30,000
Where is it?

166
00:14:36,640 --> 00:14:37,640
Comrade Fah,

167
00:14:37,840 --> 00:14:38,959
stop right now!

168
00:14:38,960 --> 00:14:40,039
Don’t take my father’s things!

169
00:14:40,040 --> 00:14:40,520
Hey!

170
00:14:40,520 --> 00:14:41,320
Don’t take them!

171
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:42,320
Bai Tong!

172
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:45,319
- Don't!
- Hey!

173
00:14:45,320 --> 00:14:46,480
This is not Comrade Ploeng’s?

174
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:48,400
This belongs to the Party.

175
00:14:51,440 --> 00:14:52,520
And what is this, huh?

176
00:14:58,360 --> 00:14:59,440
That’s enough, Comrade Fah.

177
00:14:59,960 --> 00:15:01,680
Wearing makeup and fixing hair like this...

178
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:03,200
Looks like discipline is gone now.

179
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:07,719
If I see it again, I won’t let it slide.

180
00:15:07,720 --> 00:15:09,759
In what capacity are you saying that?

181
00:15:09,760 --> 00:15:11,520
You're not the leader of the base.

182
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:14,480
Comrade Ploeng would never threaten anyone like this.

183
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:32,400
Sila.

184
00:15:38,120 --> 00:15:39,880
Mada.

185
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:48,800
Ravin.

186
00:15:49,600 --> 00:15:50,760
Chai Chan.

187
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:53,240
Police Lieutenant...

188
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:57,160
Rapee Chai Chan.

189
00:15:58,080 --> 00:15:59,199
I knew it.

190
00:15:59,200 --> 00:16:00,720
Comrade Fah.

191
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:06,040
I just got word from Comrade Roong.

192
00:16:07,680 --> 00:16:08,680
What is it?

193
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:10,720
Comrade Roong was captured by the soldiers.

194
00:16:10,920 --> 00:16:11,959
They sent word saying--

195
00:16:11,960 --> 00:16:13,400
That they want to exchange hostages.

196
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:19,600
Go get Comrade Yue to the meeting right now.

197
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:27,280
What in the actual fuck?

198
00:16:35,920 --> 00:16:38,840
You and Comrade Yue take control of them.

199
00:16:39,800 --> 00:16:40,999
Have armed men ready.

200
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,080
Lock down the area.

201
00:16:43,560 --> 00:16:44,800
If they try anything dishonest,

202
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:47,039
we’ll be ready to strike back.

203
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:48,720
Everything must be finished tonight.

204
00:16:56,880 --> 00:16:57,880
Why?

205
00:16:59,240 --> 00:17:00,240
You have a problem?

206
00:17:05,120 --> 00:17:06,800
I’ll take care of it.

207
00:17:19,040 --> 00:17:20,040
Wait.

208
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:26,440
You and Comrade Saeng

209
00:17:26,441 --> 00:17:28,081
seem a little too close, don’t you think?

210
00:17:31,400 --> 00:17:33,280
Tell me then—what should I do?

211
00:17:47,800 --> 00:17:51,799
(Ravin ChaiChan)

212
00:17:51,800 --> 00:17:53,486
(Police Lieutenant Rapee ChaiChan
Mrs. La-Or Chai Chan)

213
00:17:57,280 --> 00:17:58,680
I’m going to take this all the way.

214
00:17:59,200 --> 00:18:00,479
Hey, where are you?

215
00:18:00,480 --> 00:18:01,200
Hey!

216
00:18:01,201 --> 00:18:03,079
Where’s your boss?

217
00:18:03,080 --> 00:18:05,239
- Bring your boss out here to talk to me!
- Stop, stop! Hey!

218
00:18:05,240 --> 00:18:06,759
This bastard right here!

219
00:18:06,760 --> 00:18:07,760
Stop!

220
00:18:08,640 --> 00:18:09,679
You know what?

221
00:18:09,680 --> 00:18:12,119
Because of you, our fathers died in prison for nothing.

222
00:18:12,120 --> 00:18:14,200
They never even got a chance to prove a damn thing.

223
00:18:18,520 --> 00:18:20,719
Hey! Hey! Hey!

224
00:18:20,720 --> 00:18:22,439
Hey, come out here and talk to me!

225
00:18:22,440 --> 00:18:23,760
Watch your mouth, kid.

226
00:18:24,360 --> 00:18:26,879
The lower court ruled that your fathers were guilty.

227
00:18:26,880 --> 00:18:28,079
Why blame the police?

228
00:18:28,080 --> 00:18:29,080
How can you say that?

229
00:18:29,800 --> 00:18:31,199
And if the court overturns it and says-

230
00:18:31,200 --> 00:18:32,239
-my father was innocent,

231
00:18:32,240 --> 00:18:32,880
how are you going to take responsibility?

232
00:18:32,881 --> 00:18:36,199
The evidence was clear at the time, so I had to do my duty.

233
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:37,399
You bastard!

234
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:39,639
What the hell did you just say, you bastard?!

235
00:18:39,640 --> 00:18:40,720
Argh!

236
00:18:42,240 --> 00:18:45,440
Let me go! Let go! Let go!

237
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:48,440
Get him out of here.

238
00:18:50,360 --> 00:18:52,160
Hey, stop!

239
00:18:54,640 --> 00:18:57,640
This isn’t over, bastard! This is not over!

240
00:18:58,080 --> 00:19:00,319
I'll get you back.

241
00:19:00,320 --> 00:19:01,560
Go!

242
00:19:03,880 --> 00:19:04,880
I’ll handle it myself.

243
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:08,800
How are you going to handle it? Tell me.

244
00:19:12,200 --> 00:19:13,559
Why the hell isn’t he here yet?

245
00:19:13,560 --> 00:19:14,560
This is taking forever.

246
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:19,879
If we kill him, how are we any different from him?

247
00:19:19,880 --> 00:19:21,399
I don’t care whether we’re different or not.

248
00:19:21,400 --> 00:19:22,879
I only care that he pays for it.

249
00:19:22,880 --> 00:19:24,439
I’ll get rid of them all.

250
00:19:24,440 --> 00:19:25,960
Why are you chickening out now?

251
00:19:30,080 --> 00:19:31,200
He’s here!

252
00:19:32,480 --> 00:19:33,480
Ready?

253
00:19:33,680 --> 00:19:35,039
Wait... I’m not doing this anymore. Let’s go back.

254
00:19:35,040 --> 00:19:36,159
If you won’t do it, I will.

255
00:19:36,160 --> 00:19:37,160
You...

256
00:20:00,640 --> 00:20:01,800
Argh!

257
00:20:08,680 --> 00:20:09,680
Go to hell!

258
00:20:13,640 --> 00:20:14,640
Sin!

259
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:23,520
You!

260
00:20:23,521 --> 00:20:24,600
Don’t hurt my friend!

261
00:20:27,080 --> 00:20:28,400
Don’t hurt my friend!

262
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:01,080
Aagh! Aagh! Aagh!

263
00:21:21,640 --> 00:21:24,279
Sin! Sin! Sin! Look at me!

264
00:21:24,280 --> 00:21:25,879
Look at me, Sin!

265
00:21:25,880 --> 00:21:27,160
Sin, look at me!

266
00:21:29,280 --> 00:21:30,280
Run!

267
00:21:30,440 --> 00:21:31,440
Run!

268
00:21:31,520 --> 00:21:33,400
Run! Go!

269
00:21:33,880 --> 00:21:34,880
Go!

270
00:21:36,800 --> 00:21:37,800
Go!

271
00:21:49,480 --> 00:21:50,480
Sin!

272
00:21:52,360 --> 00:21:53,360
Or do you want him to find out

273
00:21:53,361 --> 00:21:54,681
that you and I killed his father,

274
00:21:55,520 --> 00:21:56,880
and wait for him to come after us?

275
00:22:02,680 --> 00:22:03,720
I’m telling you,

276
00:22:05,440 --> 00:22:08,040
we should nip it in the bud.

277
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:17,640
Nop.

278
00:22:21,280 --> 00:22:23,080
Whether you want to be the leader of the base

279
00:22:24,840 --> 00:22:26,719
or whatever else you want to do,

280
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:27,720
I don’t care.

281
00:22:29,760 --> 00:22:30,760
But this matter...

282
00:22:33,080 --> 00:22:34,640
Let me handle it myself.

283
00:23:19,840 --> 00:23:20,920
Hey!

284
00:23:34,480 --> 00:23:35,480
What’s wrong with you?

285
00:23:36,360 --> 00:23:37,640
Why did you hurt yourself?

286
00:23:49,760 --> 00:23:51,680
Are you so jealous that you ended up crying?

287
00:23:53,600 --> 00:23:55,840
Why are you acting like a child?

288
00:23:56,760 --> 00:23:58,800
I had a small argument with Comrade Fah.

289
00:24:00,120 --> 00:24:01,200
It’s nothing.

290
00:24:07,720 --> 00:24:08,960
Come on, I’ll treat your wound.

291
00:24:15,200 --> 00:24:16,200
Go back first.

292
00:24:17,080 --> 00:24:18,560
I’ll follow after you.

293
00:25:13,600 --> 00:25:14,760
When you get out,

294
00:25:15,960 --> 00:25:17,360
don’t ever come back here again.

295
00:25:22,200 --> 00:25:23,840
Whether I come back or not, I don’t know.

296
00:25:25,280 --> 00:25:27,600
But I’m definitely taking my person with me.

297
00:25:35,520 --> 00:25:36,840
Does Vin know

298
00:25:37,720 --> 00:25:39,000
that he belongs to you?

299
00:25:41,480 --> 00:25:42,960
Anything that’s in the wrong place

300
00:25:44,760 --> 00:25:46,200
doesn’t stay there for long.

301
00:25:47,720 --> 00:25:49,760
If fooling yourself makes you happy, then go ahead.

302
00:27:06,040 --> 00:27:08,000
Why are you sleeping here?

303
00:27:12,040 --> 00:27:13,040
I was worried.

304
00:27:13,920 --> 00:27:15,840
Did you have a serious fight with Comrade Fah?

305
00:27:19,880 --> 00:27:20,960
Go get some sleep.

306
00:27:26,760 --> 00:27:28,440
I took this from the medical hut.

307
00:27:30,080 --> 00:27:31,480
I need to hurry and return it.

308
00:27:39,880 --> 00:27:40,880
Come here.

309
00:28:40,520 --> 00:28:43,080
Even now, you’re still shy?

310
00:28:53,920 --> 00:28:55,760
Did you ever feel so happy--

311
00:28:58,080 --> 00:29:00,240
That you're afraid it ends badly?

312
00:29:01,320 --> 00:29:04,160
People either part while alive... or part by death.

313
00:29:05,360 --> 00:29:07,040
And we never know when we’ll part.

314
00:29:07,960 --> 00:29:09,319
If we spend all our time being afraid

315
00:29:09,320 --> 00:29:10,680
until we can’t do anything at all,

316
00:29:11,320 --> 00:29:12,640
wouldn’t it be more regretful

317
00:29:13,920 --> 00:29:15,480
if we never tried with all our heart?

318
00:29:28,360 --> 00:29:29,600
Then what should I do?

319
00:29:32,560 --> 00:29:34,760
You have to keep collecting happiness little by little.

320
00:29:35,280 --> 00:29:36,200
Like this—

321
00:29:36,201 --> 00:29:37,760
I'm doing it right now.

322
00:30:13,000 --> 00:30:14,000
That’s enough.

323
00:30:17,960 --> 00:30:20,240
And you don’t need to be jealous of that soldier anymore.

324
00:30:22,000 --> 00:30:23,280
I love only this person.

325
00:31:26,080 --> 00:31:27,640
The murderer is coming.

326
00:32:04,480 --> 00:32:05,480
I’m sorry.

327
00:32:56,680 --> 00:32:57,800
Go tell Vin

328
00:32:58,480 --> 00:33:00,440
that the person who loves him is waiting outside.

329
00:33:08,120 --> 00:33:09,200
You’re alright, aren’t you?

330
00:34:05,720 --> 00:34:07,719
What did that soldier say just now?

331
00:34:07,720 --> 00:34:08,880
Did you get what he said?

332
00:34:17,680 --> 00:34:19,640
Oh, Comrade Saeng, how did you get here?

333
00:34:24,680 --> 00:34:25,680
So?

334
00:34:26,200 --> 00:34:27,320
When did it start?

335
00:34:34,920 --> 00:34:36,400
Can you please not tell anyone?

336
00:34:37,760 --> 00:34:38,560
I don’t want Comrade Saeng

337
00:34:38,561 --> 00:34:39,961
to get into trouble because of me.

338
00:34:43,280 --> 00:34:45,919
The good thing about being a courier, Comrade,

339
00:34:45,920 --> 00:34:47,519
is first of all,

340
00:34:47,520 --> 00:34:49,159
I run everywhere in the forest,

341
00:34:49,160 --> 00:34:50,680
outside the forest, and in the city.

342
00:34:52,000 --> 00:34:54,319
I meet all kinds of people everywhere.

343
00:34:54,320 --> 00:34:57,479
Whether it’s couples with an age gap and things like that,

344
00:34:57,480 --> 00:34:59,360
or men who like men, women who like women...

345
00:35:00,160 --> 00:35:02,440
I honestly don’t think there’s anything strange about it.

346
00:35:04,520 --> 00:35:05,520
And...

347
00:35:07,000 --> 00:35:08,160
do you despise it, Comrade?

348
00:35:10,880 --> 00:35:13,840
I think it’s simply about two people loving each other.

349
00:35:15,160 --> 00:35:16,360
There’s nothing ugly about it.

350
00:35:18,320 --> 00:35:19,400
So what now?

351
00:35:20,440 --> 00:35:21,840
Anything to say?

352
00:35:22,600 --> 00:35:24,440
Do you love each other that much, huh?

353
00:35:28,200 --> 00:35:30,279
Wow... seeing Comrade Yue blush like this,

354
00:35:30,280 --> 00:35:31,799
I can die with my eyes closed now.

355
00:35:31,800 --> 00:35:32,800
I’m off.

356
00:35:34,040 --> 00:35:35,240
Hurry and catch up.

357
00:35:36,760 --> 00:35:38,400
Comrade Phu Pha.

358
00:36:03,040 --> 00:36:04,040
Dan.

359
00:36:04,120 --> 00:36:05,120
Father.

360
00:36:07,960 --> 00:36:08,960
How did you get here?

361
00:36:09,600 --> 00:36:11,799
Whatever you’re planning to do, just tell me?

362
00:36:11,800 --> 00:36:12,840
Is that so hard?

363
00:36:16,200 --> 00:36:17,200
If...

364
00:36:17,720 --> 00:36:20,680
If I had told you I was going in there to become a hostage,

365
00:36:21,320 --> 00:36:22,480
would you have let me go?

366
00:36:23,240 --> 00:36:24,640
And what were you doing in there?

367
00:36:26,200 --> 00:36:27,400
Helping the students.

368
00:36:28,600 --> 00:36:31,040
There are students in the jungle all over the country.

369
00:36:31,680 --> 00:36:33,720
But you deliberately chose to go to that base.

370
00:36:35,040 --> 00:36:36,399
Does this have anything to do with the information.

371
00:36:36,400 --> 00:36:37,879
I asked you to investigate before?

372
00:36:37,880 --> 00:36:39,280
Um... no, it’s not related, Father.

373
00:36:41,440 --> 00:36:43,159
As for Baan Saeng Dao Base,

374
00:36:43,160 --> 00:36:45,040
it’s the base closest to the main headquarters.

375
00:36:45,440 --> 00:36:47,720
If this place falls, the rest will collapse too.

376
00:36:48,800 --> 00:36:49,800
I just wanted to-

377
00:36:50,080 --> 00:36:51,759
-settle things properly, that’s all.

378
00:36:51,760 --> 00:36:53,200
Don’t think about attacking anymore.

379
00:36:54,120 --> 00:36:55,680
Right now, the higher-ups have a policy

380
00:36:56,120 --> 00:36:57,360
to bring the students back in.

381
00:36:57,800 --> 00:36:59,040
Bring the students back?

382
00:36:59,800 --> 00:37:00,400
Yes.

383
00:37:00,400 --> 00:37:01,400
I mean...

384
00:37:02,200 --> 00:37:04,360
Does that mean we’re not going to fight anymore?

385
00:37:05,080 --> 00:37:06,080
Yes.

386
00:37:06,720 --> 00:37:07,760
The leaders have realized-

387
00:37:08,560 --> 00:37:10,640
-that chasing each other like this

388
00:37:11,680 --> 00:37:14,000
is the same as killing our own children and grandchildren.

389
00:37:14,160 --> 00:37:15,720
Bringing them back out of the forest

390
00:37:16,880 --> 00:37:19,160
will make them useful to the nation.

391
00:37:28,440 --> 00:37:30,679
Why are you making dots like that, Comrade Saeng?

392
00:37:30,680 --> 00:37:32,560
I’m not a spotted deer.

393
00:37:39,880 --> 00:37:41,520
A spotted deer or a cat?

394
00:37:43,800 --> 00:37:45,880
Then do it properly, Comrade Saeng.

395
00:37:47,120 --> 00:37:48,519
Stay still. I’ll fix it.

396
00:37:48,520 --> 00:37:53,879
Comrade Bai Tong’s flower crown is finished.

397
00:37:53,880 --> 00:37:56,120
How is it? Look in the mirror.

398
00:37:58,720 --> 00:38:00,040
So pretty.

399
00:38:00,840 --> 00:38:04,440
Of course. Cause I made it.

400
00:38:09,480 --> 00:38:11,720
What are you doing?

401
00:38:12,680 --> 00:38:14,880
The order appointing the new base leader has arrived.

402
00:38:27,800 --> 00:38:29,639
I feel greatly honored

403
00:38:29,640 --> 00:38:31,680
to be trusted with taking care of this base.

404
00:38:32,360 --> 00:38:35,280
And I promise that everything will remain the same.

405
00:38:36,320 --> 00:38:38,239
But some loose matters may be adjusted-

406
00:38:38,240 --> 00:38:40,280
-to better follow the rules.

407
00:38:49,840 --> 00:38:51,599
And the rules begin now!

408
00:38:51,600 --> 00:38:54,719
When the leader is speaking, everyone should listen,

409
00:38:54,720 --> 00:38:56,520
not turn and look elsewhere.

410
00:38:57,600 --> 00:38:59,440
And I’d like two or three comrades

411
00:38:59,560 --> 00:39:00,799
to help me move Comrade Ploeng’s

412
00:39:00,800 --> 00:39:01,840
belongings from the house.

413
00:39:05,080 --> 00:39:06,080
Because I’ll likely-

414
00:39:06,600 --> 00:39:07,920
-be moving in there

415
00:39:08,880 --> 00:39:10,359
as required by the position.

416
00:39:10,360 --> 00:39:12,000
I’ll speak on behalf of Comrade Bai Tong.

417
00:39:12,240 --> 00:39:13,479
Comrade Bai Tong has lived there since birth.

418
00:39:13,480 --> 00:39:14,480
And?

419
00:39:14,640 --> 00:39:15,600
If moved out now,

420
00:39:15,601 --> 00:39:17,361
Comrade Bai Tong won’t be able to handle it.

421
00:39:17,840 --> 00:39:18,840
That’s right.

422
00:39:18,960 --> 00:39:20,280
Let Comrade Bai Tong rest first.

423
00:39:20,840 --> 00:39:22,239
Let her recover emotionally first.

424
00:39:22,240 --> 00:39:23,000
No.

425
00:39:23,000 --> 00:39:23,960
It must be now.

426
00:39:23,961 --> 00:39:25,319
- Why?
- Damn it.

427
00:39:25,320 --> 00:39:26,399
You really meddle too much.

428
00:39:26,400 --> 00:39:27,519
You two, follow me.

429
00:39:27,520 --> 00:39:28,520
Now.

430
00:39:28,920 --> 00:39:29,920
Hey!

431
00:39:43,160 --> 00:39:44,879
You two, move everything out.

432
00:39:44,880 --> 00:39:46,400
Don’t leave a single piece behind. Go!

433
00:39:47,360 --> 00:39:48,800
Don’t take my father’s things!

434
00:39:49,640 --> 00:39:50,840
- Hey!
- No!

435
00:39:51,480 --> 00:39:53,800
- No! Where are you taking my father’s things?!
- Bai Tong.

436
00:39:59,520 --> 00:40:01,039
Don’t take my father’s things!

437
00:40:01,040 --> 00:40:02,040
Hey!

438
00:40:06,960 --> 00:40:08,999
Don’t take anything away!

439
00:40:09,000 --> 00:40:09,760
Let go!

440
00:40:09,760 --> 00:40:10,760
Bai Tong!

441
00:40:10,760 --> 00:40:11,760
Bai Tong!

442
00:40:12,200 --> 00:40:13,599
You won’t even spare a child, huh?

443
00:40:13,600 --> 00:40:15,640
You really love meddling in my business, don’t you?

444
00:40:24,840 --> 00:40:26,160
This is already more than enough.

445
00:40:26,920 --> 00:40:28,159
Don’t make this a bigger deal.

446
00:40:28,160 --> 00:40:29,600
Why are you staring at me like that?

447
00:40:29,720 --> 00:40:31,360
Got a problem? Huh?

448
00:40:37,080 --> 00:40:38,080
Bai Tong!

449
00:40:39,120 --> 00:40:40,960
Aah! You little brat!

450
00:40:46,640 --> 00:40:47,879
Wearing makeup and fixing your hair like-

451
00:40:47,880 --> 00:40:49,560
-this is against Party rules, understand?

452
00:40:55,560 --> 00:40:56,560
Son of a bitch!

453
00:40:56,560 --> 00:40:57,560
Bai Tong!

454
00:41:01,200 --> 00:41:02,400
Ouch!

455
00:41:06,440 --> 00:41:07,440
- Bai Tong!
- Sin.

456
00:41:07,720 --> 00:41:08,840
If you don’t stop right now,

457
00:41:09,720 --> 00:41:10,759
you’ll see.

458
00:41:10,760 --> 00:41:11,840
You...

459
00:41:33,160 --> 00:41:34,319
Am I pretty, Father?

460
00:41:34,320 --> 00:41:36,120
Wow...

461
00:41:36,800 --> 00:41:38,640
very pretty, my dear.

462
00:41:39,760 --> 00:41:41,519
But you know

463
00:41:41,520 --> 00:41:44,880
you can’t wear flowers like that and go walking outside.

464
00:41:45,960 --> 00:41:47,959
But why, Father?

465
00:41:47,960 --> 00:41:49,800
I can let only Comrade Ying see it.

466
00:41:51,920 --> 00:41:55,440
If every woman comrade here wanted to be pretty like you,

467
00:41:56,200 --> 00:41:59,080
and wanted to wear flowers like you, every one of them,

468
00:42:00,120 --> 00:42:01,600
what do you think would happen?

469
00:42:04,920 --> 00:42:06,519
If all the women comrades

470
00:42:06,520 --> 00:42:08,279
picked flowers to wear every day,

471
00:42:08,280 --> 00:42:10,160
then there wouldn’t be any flowers left, right?

472
00:42:11,440 --> 00:42:12,600
That’s true.

473
00:42:13,480 --> 00:42:14,679
Flowers...

474
00:42:14,680 --> 00:42:17,439
they’re useful because they’re beautiful.

475
00:42:17,440 --> 00:42:19,440
And they have other uses too.

476
00:42:20,240 --> 00:42:21,520
But here,

477
00:42:22,120 --> 00:42:24,640
I see them as something unnecessary.

478
00:42:26,360 --> 00:42:27,760
Bai Tong, my child.

479
00:42:28,800 --> 00:42:30,639
I want you to be a good example

480
00:42:30,640 --> 00:42:32,080
to the women comrades here.

481
00:42:33,160 --> 00:42:34,520
Live simply,

482
00:42:35,000 --> 00:42:36,560
and not extravagantly.

483
00:42:37,720 --> 00:42:39,200
You understand me, don’t you?

484
00:42:45,920 --> 00:42:47,919
Then I’ll pick flowers from the ground-

485
00:42:47,920 --> 00:42:49,320
-and wear them only for Father.

486
00:42:50,760 --> 00:42:52,160
That's my girl.

487
00:42:52,760 --> 00:42:54,000
Very good.

488
00:42:54,760 --> 00:42:57,080
Very good for understanding things so easily.

489
00:43:21,160 --> 00:43:22,200
You hit me that hard...

490
00:43:22,720 --> 00:43:24,320
you really hate me that much, don’t you?

491
00:43:24,560 --> 00:43:26,320
I only asked what you two are to each other.
